- Story & Context: On August 11, 1999, just outside the carnival fairgrounds of Szeged, cook-turned-drummer Mansoor accidentally tipped a cauldron of smoking ghee into the generator pit just as the moon took its first bite of the sun. The scorching fat ignited the wiring with a shower of green sparks, forcing the brass section and sitarist to drown out the crowd's rising panic with a furious 155 BPM barrage. As the sky dimmed into sudden twilight, Mansoor grabbed a battered megaphone and howled over the screaming sitar strings: "Feed the fire with your teeth, the sky is eating itself!"
